# condor_submit_dag sweep_noise.dag : the decade at 4096 px (60 rings, hmi.M_45s) for the noise levels sigma = 8, 20,
# 50, 100 G of the magnetograms (noise_th = sigma, B_th = 3 sigma), T_sp = 487 K, ccf_norm = 2 and the Dumusque
# bisector times mu (settings_noise.sh), everything in ${BASE}/noise:
#   plage    : A_th = 0, the 7 I_th (parameters_noise_plage.txt: noise_th, B_th, I_th, A_th, Temp)
#   fraction : B_sat = 25, 50, 100, 200, 300, 500 G where larger than B_th, the 7 I_th
#              (parameters_noise_fraction.txt: noise_th, B_th, I_th, B_sat, Temp)
#   1. the grids of T_sp (build_grids_noise.sub)                                                 } at the same time
#   2. identification in 80 blocks of days per kind, the sets of its file at once (identify_noise.sub) }
#   3. the days still missing and the filling factors of every set (aggregate_noise.sub)
#   4. one simulation per line of the parameter files (run_noise_plage.sub, run_noise_fraction.sub)
#   5. per kind: table of the RMS against HARPS-N, SORCE, TSIS-1 and the figures, and the disc filling factors against
#      SATIRE-S on the days with a SATIRE mask (collect_noise.sub, satire_ff.csv of satire_ff.py satire; it runs even
#      if some sets failed)
JOB grids              build_grids_noise.sub
JOB ident_plage        identify_noise.sub
JOB ident_fraction     identify_noise.sub
JOB aggregate_plage    aggregate_noise.sub
JOB aggregate_fraction aggregate_noise.sub
JOB sets_plage         run_noise_plage.sub
JOB sets_fraction      run_noise_fraction.sub
JOB collect_plage      collect_noise.sub
JOB collect_fraction   collect_noise.sub
VARS ident_plage        kind="plage"
VARS ident_fraction     kind="fraction"
VARS aggregate_plage    kind="plage"
VARS aggregate_fraction kind="fraction"
VARS collect_plage      kind="plage"
VARS collect_fraction   kind="fraction"
PARENT ident_plage CHILD aggregate_plage
PARENT ident_fraction CHILD aggregate_fraction
PARENT grids aggregate_plage CHILD sets_plage
PARENT grids aggregate_fraction CHILD sets_fraction
PARENT sets_plage CHILD collect_plage
PARENT sets_fraction CHILD collect_fraction
SCRIPT POST ident_plage    /bin/true
SCRIPT POST ident_fraction /bin/true
SCRIPT POST sets_plage     /bin/true
SCRIPT POST sets_fraction  /bin/true
